course: dictionary
lesson: 9673
title: Successor: who or what comes next
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A successor is the person or thing that comes after and takes the place of someone or something else. Look for clues in the sentence: who was there before, and who arrives next? «Catholics see the Pope as the successor of the apostle Peter; other churches do not accept his authority.» Peter came first, and the Pope comes after him, so a successor is the one who follows.
explain: The word is about taking over. A king's successor is usually his eldest child, and Joshua was the successor of Moses. Each one takes the job or position after the person before has left it.
explain: The word also works in maths and everyday life. The successor of 9 is 10, because 10 comes right after 9. A new phone model is the successor of the old one, because it comes after it and replaces it.
fact: A successor is a person or thing that comes after and replaces someone or something else.
fact: «Successor» is a noun, so you can say a successor, or successors.
fact: In the Bible, Joshua was the successor of Moses, and Elisha was the successor of Elijah.
fact: In maths, the successor of a whole number is the number that comes right after it: the successor of 9 is 10.
fact: Useful phrases include «successor to», «a worthy successor» and «name a successor».
exercise: In maths, what is the successor of 9? | 8 | *10 | 9 | 90
exercise: «Catholics see the Pope as the successor of the apostle Peter; other churches do not accept his authority.» In this sentence, who is the successor? | *The Pope | The apostle Peter | Other churches | His authority
exercise: A new phone model is the successor of the old one. What does successor mean here? | A phone that has stopped working | A rival phone made by another company | Something older that is kept for ever | *Something that comes after and replaces the old one
test: In the Bible, who was the successor of Moses? | *Joshua | Peter | Elisha | Elijah
test: The successor of 9 is 10. What number comes just before 9? | *8 | 7 | 9 | 10
exam: A successor is someone who takes over a job, title or position after someone else leaves it. What does «successor» mean? | A king who rules for a short time | A word that means the same as predecessor | The person who leaves a job for good | *The person or thing that comes after and takes the place of another
